# TTP-2026-0163 — First-Time Kubernetes Secret Enumeration & Access (SIM-CDR-026)
# XQL paste-buffer generated by detection_scanner/scripts/export_artifacts.py

## ABIOC — Kubernetes secrets enumeration for the first time (behavioral-ML, causality-anchored)
# severity: high
# behavioral_profile: machine-learning
# causality_anchor: Per-service-account secret-enumeration baseline: the set of identities that have historically issued list/watch on the secrets resource. A first-seen subject deviates from that learned baseline.
# Analytics (first-seen ML): a Kubernetes identity lists secrets for the first time. XSIAM learns which service accounts enumerate secrets in baseline; a previously-unseen subject issuing a list-secrets call is flagged as reconnaissance. This is a first-seen anomaly over the API-server audit feed, not a parent->child causality-chain ABIOC. Keyed on the kubernetes_audit_logs API-server audit feed.

dataset = kubernetes_audit_logs
| filter verb = "list" and objectRef_resource = "secrets"
| filter user_username = "system:serviceaccount:cortexsim-canary:compromised-sa"
| comp count() as enum_events by user_username, sourceIPs, objectRef_namespace
| filter enum_events >= 1
| fields user_username, sourceIPs, objectRef_namespace, enum_events

## ABIOC — Unusual Kubernetes secret access (behavioral-ML, causality-anchored)
# severity: high
# behavioral_profile: machine-learning
# causality_anchor: Per-service-account secret-read baseline: the secrets, source IPs, and access rate a given identity normally touches. Reading a secret outside that learned profile is the deviation.
# Analytics (behavioral / ML): a Kubernetes identity reads secrets in a way that deviates from its established access baseline. XSIAM learns typical per-identity secret get/watch behavior from the API-server audit feed and flags atypical reads (new secrets, new source IP, or a spike in volume). Keyed on kubernetes_audit_logs.

dataset = kubernetes_audit_logs
| filter verb in ("get", "watch") and objectRef_resource = "secrets"
| filter user_username = "system:serviceaccount:cortexsim-canary:compromised-sa"
| comp count() as secret_reads by user_username, sourceIPs, objectRef_name
| filter secret_reads >= 1
| fields user_username, sourceIPs, objectRef_name, secret_reads

## VALIDATION — Kubernetes secret audit records observed for the run window
# purpose: validation
# dataset: kubernetes_audit_logs

dataset = kubernetes_audit_logs
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 900)
| filter objectRef_resource = "secrets" and verb in ("get", "list", "watch")
| comp count() as observed_audit_records by user_username, verb
| filter observed_audit_records >= 1
| fields user_username, verb, observed_audit_records

